cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use moe-stream in your work, please cite it as below."
title: "moe-stream: Mixture-of-Experts models bigger than RAM, streamed from SSD"
type: software
authors:
  - alias: Wok3b
version: 0.1.0
date-released: 2026-10-14
license: MIT
repository-code: "https://github.com/Wok3b/moe-stream"
abstract: >-
  An explicit expert cache for llama.cpp that runs Mixture-of-Experts models
  from an NVMe SSD on a 16 GB laptop, CPU only. Experts are read into locked
  slots with unbuffered I/O, predicted one layer ahead with the next layer's
  router, and evicted by decayed use counts, instead of being demand-paged by
  the operating system. Output is bit-exact with llama.cpp's mmap path.
  Qwen3.6-35B-A3B (20.6 GiB) decodes at 6.4 tok/s in an 8 GB memory budget,
  against 1.6 tok/s memory-mapped.
keywords:
  - mixture-of-experts
  - llama.cpp
  - llm-inference
  - expert offloading
  - nvme
  - gguf
